You check, and the dealer checks behind, so we go to showdown. Before I settle, I need to correct my earlier turns: I announced a 2♠ turn and then replaced it with the 7♦ and 5♣, so the 2♠ is missing from the board. The board I'm settling on is K♦ 9♣ 6♥ 7♦ 5♣.

The dealer's pair of eights (8♦ 8♣) beats your Q-J-10-4, which makes only K-Q-J-9-7 high. The dealer takes the 120 pot. Your bankroll stays at 950.
